{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"navigation navigation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","fileName":"Navigation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Navigation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Perception and Navigation]] [[Augmented Reality Navigation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","Multiple-Perspective Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"navigation navigation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","fileName":"Navigation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Navigation","heading":"Navigation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Navigation combines the motor and cognitive work of moving through an environment. Its motor component is [[3D Travel]], and its cognitive component is [[Wayfinding]].\n\nTravel changes the viewpoint or location. Wayfinding determines where to go and how to get there. An efficient travel method is insufficient when the user lacks the [[Spatial Knowledge]] needed to choose a route, while a good route plan is useless without a controllable way to move.\n\nDesigners can integrate the two through maps, landmarks, view overviews, or techniques that reinforce a [[Cognitive Map]] while the user travels.\n\nAR can support navigation in the traveler's own physical frame by registering points of interest, routes, and directional cues with the visible environment. A [[Multiple-Perspective Interface]] can connect this local guidance to an overview when the user also needs global route structure.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","Multiple-Perspective Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"navigation navigation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Navigation.md","fileName":"Navigation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Navigation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","3D Travel","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","Multiple-Perspective Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}